# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase backend - the only two variables the site reads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are public client configuration and are visible in the built JavaScript
# by design. The anon key grants only what Row Level Security allows.
#
# Set these two in the Vercel project settings as well. Vite inlines VITE_
# variables at build time, so production keeps the old values until you
# redeploy after changing them.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-supabase-anon-or-publishable-key"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin panel login - https://<your-domain>/admin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read by any code. This is only your own record of the login, which is why
# there is no VITE_ prefix - nothing here reaches the browser bundle.
#
# The real check is Supabase Auth, and every write is additionally gated by Row
# Level Security against the private.store_admins allowlist.
#
# Type the bare username "admin" on the login screen; the app appends
# "@noirelixir.com" because Supabase Auth identifies users by email address.
#
# To change the password: Supabase dashboard -> Authentication -> Users, or
# edit v_password in supabase/migrations/20261026231200_admin_product_management.sql
# and re-run it. Update this file either way.
ADMIN_USERNAME="admin"
ADMIN_PASSWORD="choose-a-long-random-password"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional - not needed to run or deploy the site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL  Postgres connection string, read only by drizzle.config.ts for
#               `drizzle-kit` schema tooling. Supabase dashboard -> Project
#               Settings -> Database -> Connection string. Keep it out of this
#               file unless you are actively running drizzle-kit; it grants
#               full database access.
